  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-wq1500.html",
  "prefLabel": "Env-Wq 1502.60 Significantly alter the characteristics of the terrain",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wq 1502.60 “Significantly alter the characteristics of the terrain” means to undertake any activity anywhere in the state that changes or disturbs the terrain so as to impede the natural runoff or create an unnatural runoff. Examples of activities that significantly alter the characteristics of the terrain include, but are not limited to:\n\n(a) Timber harvesting operations as covered by RSA 485-A:17, IV;\n\n(b) Earth moving activities that result in a temporary or permanent disturbance of an area that, over a 10-year period, cumulatively exceeds 100,000 square feet of area or cumulatively exceeds 50,000 square feet of area, as calculated in accordance with Env-Wq 1503.12, if any portion of the disturbance is within the protected shoreland as defined in RSA 483-B:4, XV; or\n\n(c) Steep slope projects that do not qualify for a general permit by rule pursuant to Env-Wq 1503.03(f).\n\nSource. #9343, eff 1-1-09; (See Revision Note #2 at chapter heading for Env-Wq 1500); amd by #9817-A, eff 12-1-10; ss by #12342 (formerly Env-Wq 1502.51); ss by #13758, eff 9-28-23; ss by #14079, eff 9-24-24, EXPIRES: 9-24-34; ss by #14472, eff 1-19-26, EXPIRES: 1-19-36; ss by #14656, eff 8-6-26, EXPIRES: 8-6-36 (formerly Env-Wq 1502.58)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-wq1500.html"
}
